  "description": "GridGain is built by the company that created and donated Apache Ignite, and sells an enterprise distribution with security, data-center replication, snapshots, rolling upgrades and Control Center tooling on top. GridGain 9 tracks Ignite 3's architecture (Raft, Calcite SQL, schema-driven tables) and adds features such as a columnar storage option for analytics. It is mostly used in financial services and other enterprises that want Ignite's in-memory speed with a vendor SLA. GridGain 8 remains available for customers on the Ignite 2.x lineage.",
